# PLACEHOLDER -- the Hemp Carpet on a llama: vanilla's white llama carpet, in hemp cloth.
#
# The MATRIX is vanilla `entity/llama/decor/white.png` (128x64, the llama's UV sheet)
# taken verbatim; all of it is cloth, and every pixel is retoned exactly the way hemp_wool.mctex
# retones white_wool: luminance over white_wool.png's range (212-254) onto hemp_fiber's C4A985
# (mid) to E0CBB3 (highlight). So a llama in hemp carpet wears the carpet block's own colours.
#
# The linter reads the sheet as an item and raises item findings on it; they are accepted, as on
# vanilla's own sheets.

@palette hemp_cloth
. = none
1 = 855C1D
2 = 865E20
3 = 886123
4 = 896224
5 = 926C33
6 = 97723B
7 = 9A753F
8 = 9A7640
9 = 9E7B46
a = A98859
b = AB8B5C
c = AD8D5F
d = AF8F62
e = B19266
f = B29468
g = B6986F
h = B89B72
j = B99C73
k = D6BFA3
m = D7C0A4
n = D8C1A6
p = D8C2A6
q = DAC4AA
r = DBC5AB
s = DCC6AD

@texture entity/llama/decor/hemp 128x64 palette=hemp_cloth
